From 421f9b7c42a1c7de9323a88e0904dcdba3cd4059 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "T. Kurt Bond" <tkurtbond@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 13:29:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 19/48] Strings.Replace deletes Length(source) characters

It deleted pos + Length(source), so Replace("XY", 3, s) of abcdefgh gave
abcXY. Oakwood: "Replace(src, pos, dst) has the same effect as
Delete(dst, pos, Length(src)) followed by an Insert(src, pos, dst)."

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/runtime/Strings.Mod | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/runtime/Strings.Mod b/src/runtime/Strings.Mod
index f8c7c7c9..4a96cceb 100644
--- a/src/runtime/Strings.Mod
+++ b/src/runtime/Strings.Mod
@@ -80,7 +80,7 @@
 
 PROCEDURE Replace* (source: ARRAY OF CHAR; pos: INTEGER; VAR dest: ARRAY OF CHAR);
 BEGIN
-  Delete(dest, pos, pos + Length(source));
+  Delete(dest, pos, Length(source));
   Insert(source, pos, dest)
 END Replace;
 
